{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1495999-cleaning-my-closet-the-last-countries","id":1495999,"title":"Cleaning my Closet: The Last Countries","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-10-31T12:55:22-07:00","id":1495999,"title":"Cleaning my Closet: The Last Countries","content":"Hello, Exalted Forum! ...What's left of it, anyway. I've been away for a long time since I wasn't doing anything Exalted anymore. but I still had some fanwork settings for 2e. These are not developed in as much depth as locations I wrote before such as Dzibilchan, Ollantijaya and Warrakai, but people still might find use for them. If my attempt to post them succeeds, I can tell the story of how they came to be written, assuming anyone's interested.<br /> <br /> Again: These were written in the waning days of Second Edition, when I still didn't know what Third Edition would be. Some elements will not be consistent with 3e.<br /> <br /> Please treat these locations and associated characters as copyrighted by me, subordinate to the wider Exalted coptyrights held by Onyx Path. If you want to use any of this in your own campaigns, please do. But don't refer to it in other fanwork without asking. (The Exalted Line Developer should still be able to contact me, so pass any requests through him.)<br /> <br /> Dean Shomshak<br /> Former Exalted writer, guest developer and fan","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1175-dshomshak","name":"DShomshak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"197"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-18T16:07:57-08:00","id":1500668,"title":"","content":"I'm assuming this got lost in the Forums bruhaha, any chance of seeing those?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-26T01:10:24-08:00","id":1501380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DShomshak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1495999-cleaning-my-closet-the-last-countries#post1495999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello, Exalted Forum! ...What's left of it, anyway. I've been away for a long time since I wasn't doing anything Exalted anymore. but I still had some fanwork settings for 2e. These are not developed in as much depth as locations I wrote before such as Dzibilchan, Ollantijaya and Warrakai, but people still might find use for them. If my attempt to post them succeeds, I can tell the story of how they came to be written, assuming anyone's interested.<br /> <br /> Again: These were written in the waning days of Second Edition, when I still didn't know what Third Edition would be. Some elements will not be consistent with 3e.<br /> <br /> Please treat these locations and associated characters as copyrighted by me, subordinate to the wider Exalted coptyrights held by Onyx Path. If you want to use any of this in your own campaigns, please do. But don't refer to it in other fanwork without asking. (The Exalted Line Developer should still be able to contact me, so pass any requests through him.)<br /> <br /> Dean Shomshak<br /> Former Exalted writer, guest developer and fan</div> </div> </div> </div>Quoting on the off-chance that Shomshak might notice this. Likewise, sending a PM.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2433-highpriest","name":"HighPriest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2433_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-26T06:23:03-08:00","id":1501398,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HighPriest</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1495999-cleaning-my-closet-the-last-countries?p=1501380#post1501380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Quoting on the off-chance that Shomshak might notice this. Likewise, sending a PM.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, i'm definitely not Mr Shomshak, but strongly suspect <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/332532-dzibilchan-empire-of-the-alligator-dean-shomshak\">this</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/332532-dzibilchan-empire-of-the-alligator-dean-shomshak?p=332910#post332910\">this</a> might cover up for some of what you guys are looking for.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-14T11:51:18-07:00","id":1505349,"title":"","content":"Some, but it might not be what he was referring to in the OP.<br /> <br /> Dean, let me add my vote requesting your remaining setting homebrew, please.<br /> Also, I am requesting permission to include your swamp strider and kwalko dinosaurs in my online collection of animal mounts, please. (The collection is offline for now.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-26T21:31:55-08:00","id":1531584,"title":"","content":"Holy crap, the Exalted forum isn't dead after all!<br /> <br /> I'm sorry the intended material never got posted: I thought my attempted post above just vanished into Oblivion. I only found out the forum was back because I tried giving someone a link to Dzibilchan. (And thanks for the repost, Baaldam!) So I'll try again. I just hope I can get the hang of the new forum.<br /> <br /> Like I said before, this is for 2nd edition. It's post- <i>Maters of Jade,</i> though, and since working on that book I've tried to get away from the encyclopedia-entry style of setting description in favor of more color text. I hope you'll like the result.<br /> <br /> Dean Shomshak<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1175,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1175-dshomshak","user":"DShomshak","date":". 02-27-2024, 12:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1175-dshomshak","name":"DShomshak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"197"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-26T21:48:30-08:00","id":1531585,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\">&lt;1&gt;Cervine Kalenders [part 1]<br /> <br /> In the North, most people know that elkmen often possess mystic powers and arcane lore. Thus, Osman the farmer felt little surprise when the towering figure plodded into the village of Burchin\u2019s Hold. The elkman stood a head and a half taller than any villager even without his heavy, branching antlers. As well as his gray-brown fur, the elkman wore a plain gray kilt and a blanket rolled and folded over one shoulder. Pouches hung from his leather belt. He bore a large pack on his back and a staff of twisted, lightning-struck oak in his hand. Cords bound small mirrors, beads and carved wooden amulets to his antlers.<br /> <br /> Osman feared the elkman no more than he would any peddler. Everyone knew elkmen were harmless.<br /> <br /> The elkman named himself as Kemalainen. He traded iron nails for bran mash, turnips and lodging in Osman\u2019s barn. Over the next two days, he sold a few luck talismans and cured Granny Sevda\u2019s cough. The elkman gave her grandson seeds for tonic herbs. With an inscribed iron plate and a spinning spoon, he mapped the geomancy around the village and advised farmers on auspicious locations for byres and wells. Always did Kemalainen speak softly. He let children poke at his antlers and invited them to tell him stories.<br /> <br /> That was how he learned about the ghost. Little Zulfiye drowned three years ago. Some nights, though, she came back to her former playmates and wanted them to go with her. The carpenter\u2019s son Gunduz did so last week and never came back. Kemalainen became very grave. He spoke long with the carpenter, the huntsman and other folk who knew the hills and forest. The elkman bought five small jars from Unver the potter. The next day, he plodded out of Burchin\u2019s Hold.<br /> <br /> &lt;3&gt;Wandering Thaumaturges<br /> <br /> The Cervine Kalenders are a mystic order of elkmen in the North. Not all elkmen join it, but most of them have kin who do. The Kalenders provide minor arcane services for Northern folk: medicines both alchemical and mundane, warding talismans, dowsing, spirit-dealing and the like. For many Northern villages, a wandering elkman is the only thaumaturge they may see in a dozen years. Few people worry about the Kalenders because the elkmen never take sides in wars or other disputes, and their magic seems small and safe.<br /> <br /> The Kalenders\u2019 code says they should not use their knowledge and powers for worldly gain or for violence. Kalenders can defend themselves, however, and they can accept alms or mystical materials that the order uses in rituals or to make artifacts. Some elkmen stretch these loopholes pretty far. They still avoid curses or other aggressive magic. The Kalenders\u2019 elders fear that if elkman mystics become known for meddling in human politics, war and commerce, they will attract dangerous attention to the order as a whole. It\u2019s happened before.<br /> <br /> Most Kalenders carry a geomancer\u2019s tools to map Essence flows. These traveling savants compile detailed and extensive maps of dragon lines and demesnes\u2026 including dozens of ancient manses that the rest of Creation forgot. Sometimes, Kalenders find other locations of geomantic importance. Now and then, they also need to use higher arts of thaumaturgy.<br /> -----------------<br /> <br /> Dean Shomshak</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1175-dshomshak","name":"DShomshak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"197"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-26T22:09:25-08:00","id":1531588,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\">Cervine Kalenders [Part 2]<br /> <br /> &lt;2&gt;Geomantic Wardens<br /> <br /> Kemalainen had no trouble finding the small shadowland. He thought the pit where Zulfiye drowned must have been a quarry centuries ago. Many other people must have drowned there, too. The elkman remembered tales of a local warlord who enjoyed mass drownings of his enemies; the remains of a fortress further up the hill made Kemalainen guess he\u2019d found the spot.<br /> <br /> The water in the pit seemed clear, but the bottom stayed dark even at midday. All the trees nearby were dead. Geomantic readings confirmed the elkman\u2019s suspicions.<br /> As the sun descended, Kemalainen drew a solid black circle on his brow. The elkman placed salt-crystals and a small silver nail in each of his jars, scratched Incarnate Names in Old Realm on the sides, and sealed the lids with wax. He then buried the pots around the edges of the pit and piled stones over them. With a silver-bladed knife he carved signs on the trunks of dead trees, then struck a silver nail into the center of each sign. As the last sliver of sun sank behind a hillside he spoke and his voice thundered with the power of Essence and the force of his will.<br /> <br /> <i>\u201cBy salt and silver I abjure, let mighty Zatesh shut the door! By traveled staff of lightning-tree, the road is closed by Mercury! By holy names and dauntless Sun \u2014 and by my will, the ward is done!\u201d</i><br /> <br /> \u201cBut I want my friends,\u201d the ghost-girl said plaintively as she waded soundlessly from the black water and pushed against the unseen barrier of the ward.<br /> <br /> \u201cAnd I must have children for my master,\u201d rasped a voice from behind Kemalainen. And the other ghost was upon him.<br /> <br /> &lt;3&gt;An Ancient Legacy<br /> <br /> Elkmen claim descent from Cervinus, a Lunar sorcerer of the First Age. Cervinus, the Kalenders say, was a crony of the legendary Salina and assisted in her great Working. This makes elkmen natural thaumaturges. A few elkmen even learn true sorcery, guided by the Salinan Working.<br /> <br /> Cervinus died during the Shogunate (and the Kalenders say he died hard). Before he died, he charged his offspring with guarding the Working and its expression through Creation\u2019s geomancy. The Kalenders carry on that mission.<br /> <br /> &lt;3&gt;Salinan Terminals<br /> <br /> As every professional mystic knows, the Salinan Working wove the trials of sorcerous initiation into Creation so that people could become sorcerers without the guidance of anyone else. There are many tales of Salinan-initiate sorcerers perceiving the secret of their first spell in the flight of birds or the twists in a chunk of driftwood.<br /> <br /> Places that see great concentrations of free Essence \u2014 notably, but not exclusively, demesnes \u2014 sometimes catch and materialize such epiphanies, ready for any perceptive sorcerer to learn. No mortal can explain why a particular location becomes an access-point to the Working, or why the terminal stores one spell or body of lore, and not another. (The Maiden of Secrets unhelpfully explains it as \u201cdestiny.\u201d) Kalenders say that if no one in Creation remembers how to cast a spell, the Salinan Working writes it into a terminal, but such a claim is difficult to prove or refute.<br /> <br /> A Salinan terminal holds points of spells and lore equal to twice the demesne\u2019s rating. (Terminals outside a demesne rarely hold more than one or two points of content.) One point \u201cbuys\u201d one Ability dot and one Specialty in some arcane subject. Spells cost one point per Circle of sorcery. For instance, a terminal might impart Medicine (Acupuncture +1) in the form of thorny vines that curve in the shape of Essence-flows within the human body, with spines marking the acupuncture points; or it might teach Sapphire Countermagic (costing two of the terminal\u2019s points) through the patterns revealed when a beam of light shines through a mass of crystals. Extracting information from a Salinan terminal involves use of the same geomantic Procedure used to find its Essence token. A skilled manse architect might be able to transfer the terminal into the manse as a built-in archive of mystic lore.<br /> -----------<br /> <br /> Dean Shomshak</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1175-dshomshak","name":"DShomshak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"197"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-26T22:21:05-08:00","id":1531589,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cervine Kalenders [Part 3]<br /> <br /> &lt;2&gt;At The Ashram<br /> <br /> Ou Lan took a sparrow\u2019s guise to follow the elkman thaumaturge through the hills. At last the Kalender led her to a tiny hamlet of his kind, and then to the mouth of a cave. She took the form of a rat to scurry after him. The signs carved around the cave mouth did not bar her way.<br /> <br /> The passage ended in a huge cavern. Forests of white stone icicles hung from the arched ceiling; mighty pillars of fluted stone rose from the floor, looming in the faint light of scattered oil-lamps. Ou Lan felt the Essence of the place prickling against her soul.<br /> <br /> Her elkman guide bowed deeply to an elkman with silver-gray fur who sat in a posture of meditation. In addition to small mirrors, the elder\u2019s antlers bore twisting lines of yellow, red and black pigment.<br /> <br /> \u201cHail, Balimoinen, Voice of Cervinus,\u201d said her guide.<br /> <br /> \u201cHail, Kemalo, and happy your return from walking in the world,\u201d the elder replied. \u201cBut you did not return alone.\u201d The elder slowly swung his lowered head back and forth. Ou Lan shrank behind a stone pillar and froze, but the elder stopped his slow nutation when he faced her. The painted antlers looked like two hands stretched to grab her. \u201cCome forth, Chosen of the Moon,\u201d the elder said. \u201cYour kind is not forbidden here.\u201d<br /> <br /> Ou Lan told herself she was mighty in her Exaltation and felt only\u2026 surprise. Not fear. Fear was for mortals. The young Lunar strode forth in the form of a weasel, then a bobcat, a wolf and finally her half-gull form, blue and silver Essence swirling about her and burning in brilliant spikes along her silver tattoos. \u201cHail, Balimoinen,\u201d Ou Lan said. \u201cBe not afraid\u2026 much. I require your service.\u201d The younger elkman took a step back as Ou Lan approached them. The elder sat unperturbed.<br /> <br /> \u201cI may <i>assist</i> the Moon-Chosen,\u201d Balimoinen said. \u201cIf I can. But I expect <i>assistance</i> in return. Forgive me if I seem unmoved by your glory,\u201d he added. \u201cI feel it, but I cannot see it.\u201d The elder raised his head, and Ou Lan saw his eyes were blank, polished stone.<br /> <br /> &lt;3&gt;The Kalenders and the Exalted<br /> <br /> Each ashram of the Kalenders has a caretaker. This elkman may well be a powerful sorcerer (for someone limited to the Terrestrial Circle, anyway). These are the Kalenders\u2019 only officers. Members of the order defer to Kalenders with greater seniority, lore and achievement, but only a caretaker can forbid or command another Kalender \u2014 and then only within the ashram itself. Given how easily a discontented Kalender can avoid contact with the organization in the Northern wilds, sensible caretakers rarely demand much of other members. Kalenders call these caretakers Voices of Cervinus, as they believe these elders sometimes contact an eidolon of their ancestor embedded in the Salinan Working. Certainly, long meditation on (and in) Salinan terminals seems to grant Voices unusually sensitive perception of Essence, and sometimes-oracular revelations.<br /> <br /> Cervinus gave his children a jaundiced view of the Dragon-Blooded. Events in the last thousand years did nothing to improve the Kalenders\u2019 opinion: Wyld Hunts slew many elkmen for their presumed association with the Lunar Anathema, or as Hundred Gods heretics for mediating between Northern communities and local spirits. A few Kalenders know about the Sidereal Exalted and regard them as similarly hostile to their order. That doesn't make cooperation impossible; but a Terrestrial or Sidereal may have to work at gaining trust.<br /> <br /> Kalenders readily assist the Lunar Exalted but do not casually violate their own codes for a Lunar\u2019s sake. Whether such assistance develops into a deeper alliance depends on how the Lunar treats Kalenders. In any case, the Kalenders cannot supply more than two dots of Allies, Backing, Followers, Influence or Mentor \u2014 they are too few and too scattered. A Lunar who became a strong and trusted Ally might be allowed to claim a hidden Manse.<br /> <br /> The Kalenders hold no institutional opinions about other Exalted \u2014 in the case of Solars, for instance, because they have no experience of them, while they know every Exigent is unique. They, as individuals, judge other Exalted as individuals. Kalenders are slow, however, to trust any being of power who lacks a recommendation from another Kalender or a Lunar ally: The elkmen have learned to be cautious with the unknown. Too many times, strange entities have turned out to be Fair Folk playing bizarre and deadly games.<br /> -----------<br /> And that's it for the Cervine Kalenders! Next: Riwa.<br /> <br /> Dean Shomshak</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1175-dshomshak","name":"DShomshak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"197"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-26T22:36:07-08:00","id":1531591,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">&lt;1&gt;Riwa [Part 1]<br /> <br /> About midway between the Lap and Gem, the Diamond Road crosses the plateau of Riwa. Let the caravan move on; linger instead in the plaza of Qoba, one of Riwa\u2019s seven cities. Listen to the bard, descendant of ancient princes, as he sings the <i>Riwayana</i>, epic repository of the country\u2019s history, heroes and lore.<br /> <br /> <i>Four times hath Riwa risen, ruled by mighty kings,<br /> And four times hath it fallen through the faults of men.<br /> An Age of Gold by glory gained, and lost through treacher\u2019s guile.<br /> An Age of Silver subsequent, built and lost for love.<br /> A Dragon Age of toil and greed, by plague its vices purged.<br /> A new law from the Risen King, by zealous pride undone.<br /> A Fifth and Final King shall come: Hear now the prophecy!<br /> When Riwa rises ne\u2019er to fall, from mortal fault set free.</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The <i>Riwayana</i> has five books, each taking a full day to sing, but the fifth book is not yet known. Today, the bard sings only a brief passage from the fourth book as a way to introduce Qoba\u2019s king.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">&lt;2&gt;Blood and Soil<br /> <br /> King Ruhollah stands on the high dais before his palace, his body painted black and a maguey thorn in his hand. He thrusts the spine through his earlobe, smears his hand with blood, and raises it high. A priest hands Ruhollah an ear of maize. The king then drives the thorn through his tongue and spits blood onto the dark soil that covers the platform. Finally, he lances his own manhood. He collects the blood in a small bowl and dribbles it over the skull of his grandfather. Thus does Ruhollah enact the covenant of the Risen King and proclaim himself the rightful heir: He hears the words of his ancestors, repays the earth for its life-giving bounty, and acknowledges that life comes from death. The charcoal on his body shows that his flesh comes from the Black Earth and to that darkness must return.<br /> <br /> &lt;3&gt;Colors of Earth<br /> <br /> Riwans treat black as the color of both life and death. Strips and dots of Black Earth run along the seasonal streams and ancient qanats that bring water from the mountains. Here the Riwans plant beans and maize. When Riwans die, they return their bodies to the Black Earth to nourish the soil with their flesh and the vital force of their lower souls.<br /> <br /> Yellow Earth surrounds the farmland. This land is too dry for crops but supports sheep and goats. The half-nomadic herdsmen are not quite respectable in Riwa, for they do not live on land sanctified by their ancestors. Still, they can return to their native villages each year to perform the sacred rites. Yellow is the color of wild things, the world without humanity. Shrines to elementals are painted yellow.<br /> <br /> The Fire Mountains to the west are the Blue Earth, the sky-land that brings water. Blue is the color of Heaven and a suitable hue for shrines to gods; an auspicious color, but not as good as black.<br /> <br /> To the East, the plateau ends in a maze of canyons, knife-edged ridges and badlands. Beyond this Ragged Edge stretches the great Southern Desert. Riwans call the desert the Red Earth, the evil land of sandstorms and raiders where death brings no life. Ancient fortresses guard the passes through the Ragged Edge. All seven kings should send troops to the fortresses, for so commanded the Dragon Lords of old. The watch sometimes fails because the modern kings of the city-states cannot agree about which fortress belongs to which king. Some Riwans, especially those living near the Ragged Edge, volunteer. Such wardens cannot be conscripted for other battles.<br /> <br /> The seven cities of Riwa are Borsuna, Dolawi, Orzad, Qoba, Resht, Uda and Weg\u00e1l. Of the ruined cities, the most important is Aman-Ri, first and eternal capital of Riwa. Nothing remains of the Golden King\u2019s palace except the great stepped, circular mound that supported it. Nevertheless, every king of Riwa since his reign \u2014 both high kings of old and the rulers of the schismed cities of today \u2014 crowns himself on the mound of the Golden King. They could not rule otherwise, or at least not rule in Riwa.<br /> <br /> &lt;3&gt;The Pact of Life and Death<br /> <br /> Riwans build shrines to placate various useful or important spirits, but they reserve true reverence for their ancestors. They bury their dead in the Black Earth with clothing, food and ornaments for the afterlife. After ten years, Riwans exhume the bones and pack them in clay jars. Wealthier Riwans use urns molded with death masks of the occupants. The jars of poor Riwans merely have a face sketched on the side. In return for prayers and offerings, Riwan ghosts bless and protect their living descendants. Few Riwans encounter ghosts, though. The Risen King taught this covenant of the living and the dead, but also said that each should stay in their own world. Riwa has no shadowlands, so few ghosts have easy access to the living in any case.<br /> <br /> Matters are different for nobles. Each city has several noble families. The nobles rise and fall in rank based on the number and power of their ancestral ghosts: The aristocracy of the living echoes the aristocracy of the dead. The royal family just has the strongest cohort of ghosts. New deaths can swell that cohort; Lethe shrinks it. Dynasties shift over the decades.<br /> <br /> The ziggurat of the noble dead dominates a Riwan city\u2019s plaza, overtopping the palaces of the living. Each tier of the ziggurat has crypts cut into its sides where black-glazed urns rest on altars of diorite, receiving sacrifices of incense, grain and blood. The royal family claims the higher tiers and crowning spire. The sacred ziggurat enables the dead to visit their tombs when mortals sacrifice to them, and so advise their heirs.<br /> -----------<br /> <br /> Dean Shomshak<br /> </span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1175-dshomshak","name":"DShomshak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"197"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-26T22:41:34-08:00","id":1531592,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Riwa [Part 2]<br /> <br /> &lt;2&gt;Holy War<br /> <br /> Tawia of the noble Darhune family dons the regalia of war: a breastplate, a skirt of leather strips, bracers, greaves and helm. Last she dons the silver-gilt mask of a desert jackal. The sisters in her martial order dress likewise, with masks of vulture, lizard and leopard. Tradition says that women must not fight in war, so they wear the visage of beasts instead. In their own chapterhouses, the male nobles don similar panoplies in the colors of their orders: Storm Knights in blue and white, Flame Knights in red and orange, Stone Knights in gray and brown, Maize Knights in green and yellow, and River Knights in green and blue. They paint their faces in their order\u2019s colors instead of wearing masks. The warriors march from their chapterhouses to the plaza and shout, \u201cRiwa and Qoba! Ruhollah and the Risen King!\u201d<br /> <br /> Similar ceremonies take place in Dolawi. The kings spent a month scheduling the war. Deaths among the aristocracy left both cities short of slaves, for nobles must not go alone to the Black Earth. A war enables the nobles to re-stock.<br /> <br /> Meeting in battle, knight shouts challenge to knight. They wager handfuls of conscripted peasants on their duels. Tawia wins ten soldiers as slaves for the Darhune. Only the bravest dare to wager their own lives: The victor shall sacrifice the loser to his ancestors.<br /> <br /> The second day brings the melee. Knights charge at the common soldiers of each city, striving with bola, net and mace to capture additional prisoners. The conscripts bear only padded clubs.<br /> <br /> On the third day, the two kings duel. Ruhollah loses and so must give 100 of his subjects to the king of Dolawi.<br /> <br /> \u201cMy ancestors demand more,\u201d says King Fodjour. \u201cDouble or nothing? I know it\u2019s irregular, but what can I do?\u201d King Ruhollah allows that his ancestors say the same, but suggests they simply duel for another 100 soldiers. Perhaps they shall break even.<br /> <br /> &lt;3&gt;Secret Conquest<br /> <br /> Indeed, lately the ancestors demand more every year: more incense, prayers and blood, richer funerals even for the common folk, more beasts and slaves sacrificed at the death of nobles. More wars. Everyone complies. No king would dare seem stingy: He would offend his ancestors and weaken his claim to inherit the Risen King\u2019s reign. Instead of making war once every few years, Qoba has fought two wars already this year.<br /> <br /> Nobody points out that the Risen King\u2019s law does not include Riwa\u2019s ritualistic slave-taking wars. When the Risen King departed, the lords of the seven cities elected a new high king from among their number. Sore losers turned to civil war. Kings and nobles sacrificed prisoners to strengthen their ancestors, which the ancestors endorsed for their own benefit. The Riwans eventually gave up on high kings, but the wars continued.<br /> <br /> Limited contact between the living and the dead also means that no Riwan has yet figured out that the new demands don\u2019t come from their ancestors. In fact, the First and Forsaken Lion conquered Riwa-of-the-Underworld four years ago. Most of the Riwan ghosts now labor in the Deathlord\u2019s prayer mills. He destroyed any noble ghosts whom he could not break to his will. Many of the ghosts who manifest in the mortuary ziggurats are imposters.<br /> <br /> In each city, bogus ancestors tell kings that ceremonial wars are not enough. They should train their knights and soldiers for real wars, marching north and south along the Diamond Road. Dutifully, the kings obey. Already, some launch raids against nearby tribes and villages, capturing entire populations for slaves and sacrifices. They want to be ready when the Final King appears to forge Riwa once more into a great nation\u2026 from mortal faults set free.<br /> --------------<br /> <br /> Dean Shomshak</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1175-dshomshak","name":"DShomshak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"197"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-26T22:47:43-08:00","id":1531593,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Riwa [Part 3]<br /> <br /> [BEGIN BOXED TEXT]<br /> &lt;3&gt;Tephra, That Was Anadem<br /> <br /> The nearest shadowland to Riwa lies almost 100 miles south of the plateau, along a now-disused spur of the Diamond Road.<br /> <br /> Once there was a valley between two knots of mountains, its rich soil watered by several small streams. Here was built Anadem, City of Flowers. A high volcanic mountain overlooked the flower-scented city. The folk of Anadem prayed to Heaven in gratitude and joy.<br /> <br /> Then the volcano erupted so violently as to destroy its eastern flank. A deluge of burning ash swept over the vale of Anadem in minutes, killing everyone and everything. The people had time only for brief prayers. None were delivered, for the gods are weak and inattentive; but many of the people became ghosts. Their death-prayers carried Anadem into the Underworld.<br /> <br /> The city\u2019s name died with its inhabitants. By day, the valley remains a desolation of barren gray ash where nothing moves except the wind. At night the city of Tephra appears, gray and white gables and towers rising in the starlight.<br /> <br /> Many among the living and the dead believe that someone in Anadem must have sinned a great sin to offend the volcano\u2019s god. Others suggest the god envied Anadem and destroyed the city out of spite. No one can ask the god, for no one has seen him since the cataclysm. The remains of the mountain, half a mile shorter than before, snarl toward Tephra like the jaw of a skull half-buried in the ground. Its former name is cursed and unspoken. Instead, men call it Anadem\u2019s Pyre.<br /> <br /> The ghosts of Tephra do not cultivate their ghostly ash-fields or otherwise pretend that they still live. They know they are dead. They could scarcely pretend otherwise, given the seared and seeping ectoplasmic flesh exposed by the blackened, flaking remnants of spiritual skin. The ghosts hate the living out of envy. They still pray, but now they have only one prayer that they offer to Oblivion: <i>May all gods burn.</i><br /> [END BOXED TEXT]</span></span><br /> --------------------<br /> <br /> And that's the end of Riwa. Next up: Tombolo.<br /> <br /> Dean Shomshak","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1175-dshomshak","name":"DShomshak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"197"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-26T23:08:18-08:00","id":1531594,"title":"","content":"NOTE: The old forum allowed pretty raw language. I'm not sure that's still true, so I bleeped one word. I think most of you can guess what it was from context.<br /> -----------<br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">&lt;1&gt;Tombolo [Part 1]<br /> <br /> The free city of Tombolo lives by trade. Most of the goods and services are the same as any coastal city in the West: The same fresh-caught fish and squid at the quays, the same coir mats and copra from Wavecrest, the same armor and weapons from Coral, the same nacre buttons and turtle-shell combs from the Neck; the same net-menders, chandlers and whores.<br /> <br /> Five bazaars stand out. Tombolo\u2019s Spice Market is better than most, though Azure\u2019s is larger. The Slave Market is similarly well stocked and a favorite place for the Lintha to sell their surplus. The Cloth Market is a marvel: Here see cottons and linens dyed the famous Tombolo green, as well as Wavecrest silks and Coral woolens, Delzahn mohair and Realm brocade \u2014 even the rare byssus of far Nathir, worth its weight in jade. The Wine Market sells vintages from throughout the West as well as other forms of alcohol. At the Bright Market one may purchase bangles and beads, poems scribed on plaques of agate and abalone, Gateway sets of gold and alabaster, caskets of seed-pearls and similar trinkets and treasures.<br /> <br /> But one who knows and has the right introductions may attend other markets and join in stranger commerce. In unnamed back-room shops, smiling vendors sell the skulls of ancient Dragon Kings, grimoires scribed in human blood, black death-roses that never wilt, and years of life in gossamer flasks. One may buy a new face, or a new fate. Spices and liquors of Heaven and Hell are for sale, and cloth woven of jewels, voices or dreams.<br /> <br /> Tombolans call this secret commerce the Hell Market. While some commodities come from spirits or the Fair Folk, the Underworld or Yu-Shan, much of the stock in trade comes from Malfeas. Demons walk openly in Tombolo \u2014 as befits a city ruled by a demon. Brocard, called the Hyacinth of Truth, rules the sea-girt city as its absolute master.<br /> <br /> Learned folk understand this is <i>very wrong</i> and someone should <i>do something</i>. But the Great and the Wise endure Brocard\u2019s presence in Creation. It is too useful.<br /> <br /> Like the city it rules, Brocard lives by trade.<br /> -------------</span></span><br /> <br /> Dean Shomshak","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1175,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1175-dshomshak","user":"DShomshak","date":". 02-27-2024, 02:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1175-dshomshak","name":"DShomshak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"197"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-26T23:17:35-08:00","id":1531597,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Tombolo [Part 2]<br /> <br /> &lt;2&gt;The Most Important Commerce<br /> <br /> Nelian entered Tombolo with a group of farmers. Once across the Conqueror\u2019s Causeway, she donned a messenger\u2019s kepi and the farmers promptly forgot her. She trotted past row houses and warehouses, up stairways and across bridges as she ascended to the city\u2019s higher tiers. Glancing down at the harbor from the Grand Rampart, Nelian saw ships from Coral, Wavecrest, Gannet and the Realm lining the quays. Further out, an inbound ship from Skullstone passed a fortress-crowned sea stack while the city\u2019s fishing fleet receded into the distance.<br /> <br /> Past the palazzos of citizens and the shrines of gods, Nelian reached Tombolo\u2019s central peak. Only two structures occupied this topmost tier: the palace-manse of Tombolo\u2019s master and the seven-sided, roofless structure that honored his ultimate progenitor. Its azure-framed doors stood open. Glancing inside, Nelian saw a Guildsman in red velvet lighting incense on one of the altars, but no one else. That was good. The day this fane had a priest\u2026 Nelian shuddered a moment, then hurried on.<br /> <br /> A brooch enameled with a hyacinth flower got her past a side door and its blood-ape guard. Once in the palace, Nelian doffed her cap and snagged a feather duster from a closet. Servants, clerks and guards ignored Nelian as she walked through the palace halls, since she obviously belonged there.<br /> <br /> In this way, Nelian reached the salon where a merchant in Ragara livery and a local slave-dealer sat opposite each other at a small table. Small violet flames danced a finger-length above each man\u2019s head. They glanced curiously at Nelian. So did Brocard, who stood at a third side of the table. The master of Tombolo tapped its lower left hand on the table to reclaim the traders\u2019 attention while Nelian dusted the blue porcelain medallions set in the room\u2019s white marble walls. The merchants turned back to their host and resumed their negotiations. Now and then they flinched and flickers of violet light escaped their mouths as their words strayed from exact and literal honesty. At last, the clerks waiting on a side-bench wrote out a contract in violet ink, the traders signed it, and Brocard sealed it with azure wax. The small flames went out. Another servant led the merchants from the salon. A gesture from Brocard sent the clerks away, too. Nelian sat in the chair last used by the Ragara trader. Brocard nodded in greeting.<br /> <br /> \u201cWell, demon, what do you have this month?\u201d<br /> <br /> Brocard tented the fingers of its upper pair of arms. \u201cMy informants say the Quarter Prince declared war on the Player of Games.\u201d Nelian waved it on. She\u2019d get the details, but the demon Octavian was always at war with someone. \u201cThe Apothecary of Stench found a patron in Creation.\u201d That was more interesting. The alchemist Mestrolian was less terrible than most Second Circle demons, but none could be ignored. \u201cAnd the Manse of Echoes Ascending...&quot; Brocard paused expectantly.<br /> <br /> Nelian leaned forward. \u201cYes?\u201d<br /> <br /> The demon tapped its fingers together, amethyst nails glittering, and smiled. \u201cAh, fate-weaver, news of an Unquestionable costs more than the Bureau\u2019s forbearance. What news do <i>you</i> bring from Heaven?\u201d<br /> <br /> &lt;3&gt;The Free City\u2026<br /> <br /> The city of Tombolo consists of a small but mountainous island half a mile from the largest island in the Tidemont archipelago. During the Shogunate, the little island was carved into a city of narrow streets connected by stairways. Bastions, gates and ramparts made the entire city a fortress. Outlying reefs became breakwaters for a great harbor. Smaller forts crowned steep islets even further from the shore. At this time, the city\u2019s name was Tenshu-Daketsu, the Fortress Mountain-Harbor.<br /> <br /> In the Six Island War two centuries before the Great Contagion, the daimyo Chagan Ugona conquered Tenshu-Daketsu. He could not take the city by sea, so his forces built a causeway from the main island. Over the centuries, silt accumulated along the causeway to create a narrow strip of land. The poorest folk of Tombolo live on this low-lying isthmus. Every few years, storm surges wash away dozens or hundreds of shacks and hovels; but there are always more poor people ready to rebuild.<br /> <br /> The Scarlet Empress occupied the city, by then called Tombolo, as one of the Realm\u2019s first conquests in the West. She lost it during the war against the Anathema Jochim when various Western satrapies took the chance to rebel. In the complicated peace negotiations that followed, Tidemont became sovereign but its new Dragon-Blooded aristocrats agreed to a power-sharing agreement for Tombolo. The co-dominium broke down within a decade. When the fighting stopped, there was a demon in charge.<br /> <br /> &lt;3&gt;\u2026And Its Master<br /> <br /> The Hyacinth of Truth should not have compelled certain citizens of Hell to speak without lies. Its own Third Circle progenitor Erramun, the Dust Ulema, sought to destroy it and grow a new Messenger Soul. Brocard fled Malfeas and took refuge in Creation. The Bureau of Destiny soon found it \u2014 but Brocard made a deal. In return for sanctuary, it provides information about the Demon Realm. The Sidereals even let it occupy and rule the war-ravaged city of Tombolo.<br /> <br /> Mere forbearance by the Sidereals would not protect Brocard from its progenitor\u2019s will and assassins sent from Malfeas. The Hyacinth of Truth buys allies back in Hell by providing information about Creation and \u2014 rarely \u2014 Heaven.<br /> <br /> Brocard\u2019s power to compel honesty goes beyond forcing people to tell the literal truth (as best they know it). It can hallow a bargain so that those who break their side of the deal wither and die with dust in their veins. Merchants usually settle for assurances of an honest intent to fulfill a contract.<br /> <br /> The Hyacinth of Truth can also stride through the air, extending its six spider-like legs into stilts of violet fire hundreds of yards long. Pirates who raid Tombolo quickly find their rigging aflame. Thus does Brocard assure the safety and prosperity of Tombolo.<br /> -----------------<br /> <br /> Dean Shomshak</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1175,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1175-dshomshak","user":"DShomshak","date":". 02-27-2024, 02:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1175-dshomshak","name":"DShomshak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"197"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-26T23:34:55-08:00","id":1531598,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Tombolo [Part 3]<br /> <br /> &lt;2&gt;Powers and Players<br /> <br /> Vozor tapped a plump finger on the azure-edged papyrus. \u201cMake your marks here by your names. Your lovely daughter is mine, confectioner, and my protection is yours once more. So long as you pay <i>on time</i>.\u201d He smirked at the woman who wore her smock half-open, with a ribbon in her hair. \u201cSmile, my dear. Your family will be safe. And some girls learn to enjoy the sesselja\u2019s changes.\u201d<br /> <br /> The gray-haired man bent over Vozor\u2019s desk \u2014 but instead of grasping the proffered pen, he flicked his hands and transparent chakrams of Essence-hardened air slashed into the throats of Vozor\u2019s guards. Before the dying guards hit the ground, the man slammed Vozor face-first into the wall. The confectioner\u2019s image unraveled in threads of Essence. In his place stood a younger man clad in saffian, silk and silver-blue mail. Mela\u2019s blue-white light shone about him, and a breeze ruffled his blue-black hair. Meanwhile, the young woman barred the office door.<br /> <br /> \u201cThe Exigency, whoremaster,\u201d Ledaal Torino said pleasantly. \u201cYou know who\u2019s selling it. Tell me or die.\u201d<br /> <br /> Vozor struggled in the Dynast\u2019s grip. \u201cI am a citizen!\u201d he ground out. \u201cBrocard will avenge me!\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOnly if I\u2019m still here when he finds out,\u201d Torino replied. A dagger of air appeared in his free hand. He pressed below Vozor\u2019s double chin. \u201cSpeak quickly, demon-f***er.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cPlease, Prince of the Earth,\u201d Vozor whimpered. \u201cI am watched. I will die if I speak to you!\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWhich way do you live longer?\u201d Then an eye opened amid the oiled ringlets at the back of Vozor\u2019s head and glared at Torino. The Dynast felt faint as a cold, alien will pressed against his mind. His grip slacked for only a moment. <i>I bear the blood of dragons. Such deviltry does not defeat me!</i> Cold air swirled around him, blowing papers through the room. \u201cNot that easy, whoremaster.\u201d<br /> <br /> Vozor screamed. Torino swore as the eye sank into Vozor\u2019s head and blood gushed from the hole. The Dynast stabbed into the wound, hoping to kill the <i>thing</i> before it killed the Tombolan. Too late.<br /> <br /> Guards pounded on the door. \u201cGet the blood-ape!\u201d one called. Torino\u2019s lips tightened.<br /> <br /> \u201cSorry, sweetling,\u201d he told the young woman. \u201cSaving your family might be a little harder than I thought.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cBut a deal\u2019s a deal,\u201d Nelian replied, making her voice shake a little. \u201cMaybe Vozor has something written about that Exy-thing. Maybe we can find it before they bring the demon.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cBrave heart!\u201d Torino said, smiling, and began tossing the room.<br /> <br /> Nelian did not smile. Bureau policy said to keep Torino thinking she was a simple tradesman\u2019s daughter he had used to reach Vozor \u2014 and that his learning of the Exigency had been chance. The eye in the back of Vozor\u2019s head, though, was pelagial work. <i>If those creatures have an Exigency\u2026</i> For stakes this high, she might need a partner, not a dupe.<br /> <br /> &lt;3&gt;Citizens, Clients, Strangers and Slaves<br /> <br /> Tombolo has a simple government called the Dominate. The law is whatever Brocard says at the time. Seven human deputies oversee particular fields of concern such as state violence (defending the city and arresting lawbreakers) or collecting and disbursing funds. Brocard endorses everything its deputies do \u2014 until it doesn\u2019t, at which point deputies may be summarily executed. That was the deal Brocard offered.<br /> <br /> The Deal underlies Tombolan law. No Tombolan has any obligation to any other, except what they spell out in a signed or witnessed contract. Even rights to life and property come only through purchase from Brocard (costing Resources \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 per year). Such persons become citizens. Everyone else can be robbed, raped, cheated or slain with impunity\u2026 unless they find a citizen willing to subcontract their protection. How /much/ protection a citizen grants, and what he demands in return, is up to the parties involved. Who does not buy protection, or have the strength to protect himself, becomes a slave to whoever has the power to take and hold him. Tombolans call this \u201cLiberty.\u201d<br /> <br /> Visitors can buy temporary protection at a weekly cost of Resources \u2022. In return, they can buy and sell in Tombolo\u2019s markets, and shall not be enslaved \u2014 but Brocard promises nothing more. A pin or patch of a hyacinth flower marks such protected strangers. Forging a pin infringes on Brocard\u2019s rule and carries the death penalty.<br /> <br /> The law of Tombolo extends to all. Citizens can summon demons as they will, but demons can buy citizenship or patronage just as humans can. So can gods, elementals, Fair Folk or anyone else: The Hyacinth of Truth treats everyone the same.<br /> <br /> &lt;3&gt;Watchers<br /> <br /> &lt;n&gt;In a squalid waterfront tavern, a Guildsman and a Lintha captain plot a slave-raid on the Gannet Isles. The sodden, snoring sailor in a corner booth is actually wide awake and memorizing every word for the All-Seeing Eye. The rat scrounging crumbs under the bar is a Lunar who seeks the identities of the Realm\u2019s agents in Tombolo. The bartender shivers briefly as he steps through the ghost that has followed the rat for days. Unseen by all but the ghost, an undertow wends its way through the tavern, sensing everyone\u2019s Essence as well as looking for merely mortal spies. The small god works for the Guild: The Guildsman cares less about the slaves to be gained than about who responds to the information he planted.<br /> <br /> Tombolo is <i>packed</i> with spies. Many interested parties want to trade with or spy on Malfeas, the Bureau of Destiny, and each other. The Great Houses of the Realm place agents in Tombolo. So does the Guild, Skullstone, Coral, the Pearl Court and every major Western nation or supernatural faction that\u2019s organized enough to have agents. Pelagothropes, People of the Sea and pelagials rise from the water on moonless nights to pursue their own secret dealings.<br /> <br /> In a city where loyalty is just another commodity for sale, very few people are only what they seem. Artisans, laborers and guards spy on their citizen protectors and sell what they learn to secret patrons \u2014 though a prudent citizen can use such channels to spread disinformation. It\u2019s also rarely in a spy\u2019s interest to be too rigid in her loyalties: So often, the person best able to help a mission is the enemy of an enemy\u2026 until the inevitable betrayal or discovery of true identities and agendas. In the city ruled by the Hyacinth of Truth, the games of deceit never end.<br /> --------------<br /> <br /> And that's it for Tombolo. Next and last: the Zanichka. But it's getting late, so I'll post it tomorrow.<br /> <br /> Dean Shomshak</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1175-dshomshak","name":"DShomshak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"197"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-27T09:25:24-08:00","id":1531626,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">&lt;1&gt;The Zanichka<br /> <br /> It is said that ten thousand tribes dwell in the great Eastern woodlands, and only Huntress Luna and far-traveled Mercury know them all. Jinru Rose-of-Dawn believed it. After 20-some years of gathering rare herbs and animals as a voyageur of the Guild, she knew that every few dozen miles brought a new tribe\u2026 human or otherwise. She had treated and traded with folk who dug their homes beneath tree roots and folk who lived in baskets hung from high branches; folk who trained bats to gather nuts and folk who fished for pythons; cat-folk and rat-folk and parrot-folk too, tribes cross-bred with animals or warped by the Wyld. Her husband and children were part of a tree-folk tribe, emerald-skinned and monkey-toed, more at home in the forest canopy than on the ground.<br /> <br /> Jinru also dealt with spirits. She opened her veins for wood spiders and offered nectar laced with opium to butterfly-gods, played the flute to charm vinerunners and buried piglets to appease trufflemasters. She once murdered one of the Fair Folk, a memory that made her smile; and she once destroyed a ghost, a memory that made her shudder. Jinru preferred humans to spirits. At least <i>some</i> humans were sane.<br /> <br /> As Jinru walked from branch to branch hundreds of feet above the ground, she wondered where her own wits had gone. She was good in the trees for someone city-born, but clumsy compared to her tree-folk companions, and getting old for such adventures. They indulged Jinru\u2019s slow, careful pace because her husband was now second-chief and because she enriched the tribe with metal tools, glass beads and brightly colored cloth traded from the Guild. Other tribes wanted a piece of the action. So did younger voyageurs. Her trading network grew.<br /> <br /> A month ago, Jinru\u2019s junior associate Sinan Greengage brought word of a new tribe. A <i>huge</i> new tribe. Moreover, these \u201cZanichka\u201d people had abundant solar mistletoe, the best drug for treating consumption. They would not deal with Sinan, though \u2014 only with Jinru, the far-famed bringer of treasures. And that was why she and Sinan moved through the treetops 60 miles from Jinru\u2019s home, with death if she missed her footing.<br /> <br /> Three hunters challenged Jinru\u2019s group. Like her companions, they were tree folk armed with spears and darts. Unlike the tree folk she knew, the hunters wore breastplates of knotted cord and slices of some lustrous brown wood that Jinru did not recognize. The Wyld had touched them, too: Instead of hair, fine green vines grew on their heads. One hunter had small white flowers in his vine-hair. Another had tiny red berries. The third had a short, sparse beard; it was dark green but otherwise normal hair.<br /> <br /> Jinru offered glass beads and an iron knife to prove her identity. The hunters accepted the gifts and gravely invited her to their village. She had found the Zanichka.<br /> <br /> As she crossed to another tree, Jinru finally identified the wood of the hunters\u2019 breastplates. She was in a miles-high chestnut tree. The wood came from chestnut hulls\u2026 but the nuts of /these/ trees were ten feet wide. Gathering them, she thought, must be a hell of a chore with only stone and bone tools. But what a food supply! The Zanichka had more than nuts, too: Jinru saw normal-sized grape vines and beanstalks growing in soil-filled cracks and hollows of the branches. She also saw a woman feeding pigeons kept in wicker cages.<br /> <br /> <br /> she came at last to the village: A long row of domed huts along a branch wide as a boulevard, each hut a single chestnut hull. At the end stood a larger hut made from nutshell sections laced together with vines. Her guides asked Jinru, Sinan and their tree folk guides to wait there while they gathered the elders.<br /> <br /> &lt;3&gt;Facts of Zanichka Life<br /> <br /> The Zanichka live in 11 gigantic chestnut trees. Each tree supports several dozen villages. Each village consists of three to eight septs, or extended families of a few dozen individuals. The tribe\u2019s total population numbers in the tens of thousands, made possible by an abundant food supply.<br /> <br /> The Zanichka wear close-fitting harnesses of macram\u00e9 with nutshell plates to protect vital areas. They make ornaments from feathers, fur, animal teeth and carved wood and bone. Zanichka obtain stone for knives and clay for hearths from the ground but must travel many miles to do so.<br /> <br /> Daring hunters travel 40 miles or so to reach the Bordermarches of the Wyld. They may find glittering treasures such as golden seedpods or glass mushrooms. Obtaining such treasures brings great prestige to a hunter. Suffering mutation, however, brings a sentence of death.<br /> <br /> Vine-hair is a hereditary mutation among the Zanichka. Once a year, though at different times for different people, the vines grow small, sweet red berries. Offering a berry is a deeply intimate gesture, usually done only between lovers.<br /> -------------<br /> <br /> Dean Shomshak</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1175-dshomshak","name":"DShomshak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"197"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-27T09:34:13-08:00","id":1531629,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Zanichka [Part 2]<br /> <br /> &lt;2&gt;Politics in the Palaver House<br /> <br /> Chilan-Yoben Ah Winituk pondered strategy as he listened to the arguments of his fellow elders. The elder woman from the distant tribe said she had many treasures to trade \u2014 best of all, metal, which Winituk had seen only on an Eastern hunt in his rash youth. He would vote for trade in a heartbeat, if it were only up to him and the good of the Yoben sept.<br /> <br /> But it wasn\u2019t that simple. Chilan-Mohinder Ix Bolcla argued passionately for alliance with the bringer-of-treasures. Last week, Bolcla had broken her word to Winituk: He voted for increasing her sept\u2019s hunting territory; but she then voted against his scheme for sharing out the healing mistletoe berries. Winituk could not let that betrayal pass lightly.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, the garden society elder Chac Ah Ramanchup argued against the alliance. He said that gathering herbs and animals for trade meant less time tending the gardens, and so less food. The children would suffer for it. Winituk knew the elder\u2019s real reason: The hunting society would gain power by supplying the herbs, and the weaving society would gain by supplying talismans against mad-storms. The garden society would lose influence by comparison. Winituk liked Ramanchup, but he also owed a favor to Chac Ix Chamra for bringing Winituk\u2019s niece into the weaving society. In another 20 years, his niece might know the powerful secrets of weaving talismans, to the benefit of the Yoben sept. Winituk would not lightly vote against the weaving society\u2019s interests.<br /> <br /> Winituk also considered Nojoch-Nur Ix Palchuah, priestess of their tree\u2019s dryad. Great Nur could protect her tree and everyone living in it from mad-storms, so the garden society did not care about talismans. In this vote, Palchuah and Ramanchup were natural allies against Chamra. Palchuah might also fear for lessening Nur\u2019s influence compared to\u2014<br /> <br /> A spasm of coughing interrupted Winituk\u2019s strategizing. When he lowered his hand from his mouth he saw it flecked with bloody sputum. <i>Oh great Nur, protect me!</i> But the dryad had no power over disease. For that, Winituk must go to the healing society\u2026 and the new god, the god of the golden berries.<br /> <br /> He glanced around the palaver-house. His fellow elders inched away from him while still squatting on the floor, trying not to be obvious and failing. The stranger woman Jinru looked at him shrewdly. She pressed a hand to her back, groaned slightly, and asked if the esteemed elders could postpone further discussion. She was still fatigued from her journey. Politely, the elders accepted Jinru\u2019s suggestion. Everyone rose. Family gossip replaced debate. Winituk knew the gossip mattered just as much as the arguments as a way to suggest alliance, opposition and reminders of favors given or owed. The stranger Jinru, he saw, still listened intently. Noticing his regard, she tilted her head and mouthed, <i>Speak to me later.</i><br /> <br /> Jinru had listed the golden berries, which she called solar mistletoe, as one of the healing herbs that interested her. New disease, new god, new cure\u2026 new visitor who was also interested in the cure? Winituk did not know how it all fit together, but he felt sure that it did.<br /> <br /> &lt;3&gt;Societies, Septs and Secrets<br /> <br /> Male and female Zanichka use the same set of names. They show gender through a prefix, <i>Ah</i> for men and <i>Ix</i> for women. (People don\u2019t use the prefixes in casual conversation.)<br /> <br /> Septs take their names from revered ancestors. The head of the extended family takes the title of <i>Chilan,</i> with the ancestral name: Thus, Chilan-Yoben Ah Winituk is Winituk, male elder of the Yoben sept. Every sept has its own tales, songs and family recipes that it keeps secret from other Zanichka. Marriages usually happen between septs, the husband joining his wife\u2019s family but swearing never to reveal one sept\u2019s secrets to the other. Such infidelity would disgrace him to the entire village.<br /> <br /> Four secret societies draw their members from all the septs. Many Zanichka belong to a society as well as their sept. The societies themselves aren\u2019t secret, but they guard their own songs, legends, techniques and lore as jealously as the septs guard their ancestral tales. Society elders might know a few Procedures of Thaumaturgy and win the title of <i>Chac</i> as a result.<br /> <br /> \u2022 The hunting society practices that important art and defends the village from dangerous animals and foreign attackers. It teaches Procedures from the Art of Husbandry, the better to attract wild game and ward off predators. Hunters also conduct most of the expeditions in search of raw materials, as they have the most experience at traveling beyond the chestnut grove and are best able to defend themselves.<br /> <br /> \u2022 The healing society prepares drugs and medicines, some of them occult drugs from the Art of Alchemy. Its members also deal with social and spiritual ailments such as persistent grudges between villagers.<br /> <br /> \u2022 The weaving society makes baskets, nutshell armor, ceremonial robes and other accoutrements. Chacs craft a variety of warding talismans through the Art of Enchantment, particularly talismans meant to protect against the Wyld and warn of its incursions. Talismans all take the form of elaborate knots of plant fiber, animal hair and feathers, hung with animal claws and other ornaments.<br /> <br /> \u2022 The garden society tends the vines and other crops. Garden society members may learn the Art of Weather Working.<br /> <br /> The Chacs and Chilans form the village council along with the <i>Nojochil,</i> the priest or priestess of the tree\u2019s dryad. Decisions are made by majority vote.<br /> --------------------<br /> <br /> Dean Shomshak</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1175-dshomshak","name":"DShomshak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"197"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-27T09:40:07-08:00","id":1531630,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Zanichka [Part 3]<br /> <br /> &lt;2&gt;Divine Extortion<br /> <br /> Nojoch-Nur Ah Naginder climbed up the trunk of his home tree, fingers and toes easily grasping bark and vines. After a few hours and several rests he reached the high, sunlit cluster of branches that his goddess Nur favored. Priests and priestesses already waited. More arrived in the next hour. Nur had called a conclave of all her Nojochils.<br /> <br /> It wasn\u2019t the only conclave in the great tree that week. The Chacs of each society held their own meetings to discuss the offer of the woman from afar. Naginder rarely wondered what the Chacs did at their conclaves \u2014 beyond arguing, of course. The societies were entitled to their secrets, just as were the septs and the priests.<br /> <br /> At last, the dryad herself appeared, her skin the hue of bark and her head crowned with chestnut leaves. The Nojochils knelt and gave the prayer of greeting. Then they got down to the arguing\u2026 very careful, gentle arguing when they argued with their god.<br /> <br /> Nur was angry. The Zanichka should pray to her alone! Did she not house them, feed them, protect them from the Wyld? That this upstart god Sundrop Breath-Of-Life demanded worship was an outrage!<br /> <br /> The priests assured the dryad of their love and loyalty. Three who were in fruit offered berries from their heads, which mollified Nur somewhat. But Nur could not cure the bloody cough that spread through the Zanichka. The new god could, through the golden berries. Sundrop Breath-of-Life said they could be free of the disease if his little bush grew in the bark of the chestnut trees; but to grow so many bushes at once he would need many prayers. What else could they do? The bloody cough killed slowly. Victims became a burden on their septs long before they died. The Nojochils pleaded for Nur not to withhold her gifts. Her faithful Zanichka could not be asked to choose between loyalty and life!<br /> <br /> A priestess rose to speak, introducing herself as Nojoch-Nur Ix Palchuah. Her village hosted the stranger, this Jinru Rose-of-Dawn whose skin was not green. The stranger wished to meet the great and generous Nur. She had sent gifts with Palchuah and hoped to present other gifts in person. It was possible, this Jinru said, that some arrangement could please everyone\u2026<br /> <br /> &lt;3&gt;Zanichka Religion<br /> <br /> The Zanichka revere the ancestors of their septs, but they do not pray to them. They want nothing to do with ghosts. If a ghost appears to her descendants, the sept\u2019s Chilan must persuade the honored ancestor to be honored in the Underworld, where the dead belong.<br /> <br /> Only the dryads of the giant chestnut trees receive regular worship in the form of chanted prayers and animal blood. As a group, the dryads call themselves the Kastanea. While they owe fealty to the region\u2019s forest walker, the Kastanea are for all practical purposes a spirit court of their own: With so many devoted worshippers, the dryads can afford to blow off most other Terrestrial gods. Over the centuries, local gods and elementals made their own deals with the Kastanea to receive minimal prayer \u2014 one day a year, no more \u2014 in return for not harassing the Zanichka.<br /> <br /> Sundrop Breath-of-Life is not one of these local spirits. This god of solar mistletoe learned to create the disease his parasitic little shrub cures. He inflicts consumption on the Zanichka. Then he offers the berries as cures\u2026 well, <i>auctions</i> them for prayer. For enough prayer, he makes solar mistletoe grow in a convenient tree. Smaller tribes around the Zanichka already pray daily to Sundrop.<br /> -----------------<br /> <br /> Dean Shomshak</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1175-dshomshak","name":"DShomshak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"197"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-27T09:47:51-08:00","id":1531631,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Zanichka [Part 4]<br /> <br /> &lt;2&gt;Departure<br /> <br /> After a month with the Zanichka, Jinru and Sinan began the long journey back to her tribe. She had a deal. Sundrop Breath-of-Life had his worshippers. The Kastanea were appeased, for now. Baskets of golden mistletoe would flow from the Zanichka to Jinru, and from her to the Guild. In return, the Zanichka would receive tools, cloth, beads and baubles a tenth the value of the medicinal berries. The Guild would soon have an outpost in the chestnut trees, from which voyageurs could explore even further and deeper \u2014 all the way into the Wyld. Sinan burbled in admiration of Jinru\u2019s negotiating skill. But her persuasions and promises still tasted foul in Jinru\u2019s mouth.<br /> <br /> <i>What\u2019s wrong with me? The Guild profits. I profit. Even the Zanichka profit. We are not using them. Not cheating them. We\u2019re not!</i><br /> <br /> <i>But Sundrop Breath-of-Life is.</i><br /> <br /> She\u2019d heard of the racket before: Cause a disease, then sell the cure. Other gods did it. Uncomfortably, Jinru knew that some Guildsmen did, too. It was the way of the world. You couldn\u2019t blame anyone for taking advantage. If you didn\u2019t, someone else would.<br /> <br /> <i>Not to my people, they don\u2019t.</i><br /> <br /> When had the Tree Folk become her people? The Zanichka weren\u2019t even her tribe. Her <i>husband\u2019s</i> tribe.<br /> <br /> <i>My children have green skin</i>.<br /> <br /> Jinru\u2019s lips tightened. The deal was good for the Guild, but it could be better for the Zanichka. Jinru\u2019s sponsor in the Guild, the great Doctor Alethia, knew more about medicines than anyone else in the Hundred Kingdoms. Aye, and more about poisons, too. Jinru would send the Dragon-Blooded doctor a special request.<br /> <br /> <i>I have killed the Fair Folk and a ghost. Let\u2019s see if I can kill a god.</i><br /> -------------</span></span><br /> <br /> And that's it for the Zanichka, and from the back of my closet. I hope you've enjoyed these societies and find them useful. I'll stick around for a few days in case anyone has questions.<br /> <br /> Dean Shomshak","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1175-dshomshak","name":"DShomshak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"197"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-27T11:00:01-08:00","id":1531634,"title":"","content":"This is solid stuff, please keep posting it here. Discord is great for immediate communication, but lousy for looking things up later.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}